.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Defines a contract for objects that can be converted into a raw byte representation suitable for hashing, serialization, or low‑level processing\&. 

The interface is intentionally minimal: any type implementing \fRIHashable<T>\fP must provide a deterministic and stable \fBToBytes\fP method\&. The returned byte sequence is used by \fBSystemEx\fP hashing algorithms and must remain consistent across platforms and runtime sessions\&. 

.PP
\fBExample:\fP
.br
 A type implementing both \fRIHashable<T>\fP and a hash attribute: 

.PP
.PP
.nf
[HashAlgorithm(typeof(Bernstein))]
public class Foo : IHashable&lt;Foo&gt;
{
    public FixedVector&lt;byte&gt; ToBytes()
    {
        // Convert internal fields into a deterministic byte array\&.
        return new FixedVector&lt;byte&gt;( \&.\&.\&. );
    }
}
.fi
.PP

